{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Plot Legend.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Plot Legend.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"plot legend plot legend","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Plot Legend.md","fileName":"Plot Legend.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Plot Legend","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-06 18:44\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Health Data Visualization]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Health Data Visualization","analyzinghealthdatainrforsasusers.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Plot Legend.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Plot Legend.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"plot legend plot legend","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Plot Legend.md","fileName":"Plot Legend.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Plot Legend","heading":"Plot Legend","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"A plot legend maps visual encodings such as color, symbol, fill, or line type to substantive categories. Its ordering must match the ordering used to draw the data, or the graph will communicate the wrong group identities.\n\nPlacement and scale should preserve the data region. When several lines are overlaid, the legend should repeat the same widths, colors, and line types used in the plot rather than rely on a separate default style.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Health Data Visualization","analyzinghealthdatainrforsasusers.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Plot Legend.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Plot Legend.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"plot legend plot legend","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Plot Legend.md","fileName":"Plot Legend.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Plot Legend","heading":"References","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"[[an